<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">pathfinder</ansi>

Pathfinder is a ranger's skill. A pathfinder walking with your company
finds easier going across rough ground, so every member pays less
strain for each step (strain is the Fatigue walking costs; <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The numbers</ansi>

  5% less strain per level, 20% at level 4, on any ground harder than a
  road (forest, swamp, snow, mountains...). It never makes ground
  cheaper than a road, and roads and settlements are left as they are.

<ansi fg="command">strain</ansi> shows it: the room's strain already includes it, and a line
names your pathfinder. It changes no journey's duration and no shared
time.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Usage:</ansi>

  There is no command: it happens as you walk.
  <ansi fg="command">autoskill pathfinder off</ansi> stops it.

The Pathfinder elite class of the rogue's Scout route is another thing: see
<ansi fg="command">help elite-pathfinder</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help survival</ansi>.
